id: pm-rl-eval-acceptance-fixtures
title: Repair the standalone evaluation acceptance fixtures
description: Packed Node 26 replay of the public main tracker reproduces failures before and after the PR #190 report fix. evaluation-plan.acceptance.ts registration returns rl_identifier_invalid. worst-cohort.acceptance.ts and shadow.acceptance.ts return process_identity_unavailable with their Git-free PATH. Match the standalone fixtures to the current identifier and process-identity contracts.
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-20T05:22:12.394Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T16:01:43.441Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "All three standalone fixtures (evaluation-plan.acceptance.ts, worst-cohort.acceptance.ts and shadow.acceptance.ts) pass when run against a packed extension and an immutable public tracker snapshot, with Git absent from the CLI PATH."
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T15:46:34.705Z",codex-sol,Round FB is replaying the three standalone fixtures against a packed extension and an immutable public tracker. The CLI PATH will contain Node only.
  "2026-11-20T15:50:52.156Z",codex-sol,"Root cause: the evaluation fixture used a repository unit with a colon and slash, and the cohort and shadow fixtures omitted the native process-birth tool (getconf on Linux) from PATH. Reused the platform identity helper. First packed Node 26 run passed all three against the archived read-only public commit 4e83f2c26e93558ca8f43e6b5e39c7d3c22e9581. The Node 26 release-checks job now invokes the same replay on code changes."
  "2026-11-20T16:01:31.003Z",codex-sol,"Node 26.13.0 passed the fixed-plan, protected-cohort and shadow packed commands with Git absent throughout the CLI PATH, including package install. The source snapshot at 4e83f2c26e93558ca8f43e6b5e39c7d3c22e9581 contained 149 items, remained read-only and kept the same digest. The workflow contract tests passed 6 of 6."
